": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!"}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: <span class=\"bullet\">Listen to the audio.</span> <span class=\"bullet\">\nOrganize the mystery sentence.</span> <span class=\"bullet\">Move each word to place it in the correct order.</span> \n</br>You have 2 attempts to submit your answers.\n", "type": "text"}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}]}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "What Is Object Oriented Programming?", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about object oriented programming.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe the development and software programming in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands key information in simple written and spoken texts about topics related to software programming and its history.  Recognizes basic ideas on programming concepts and programming history in both written and spoken passages.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Present Continuous Tense in Negative Statements", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "The <strong>Present Continuous</strong> is used to talk about actions that happen at the moment of speaking. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "To express that an action is taking place now, follow the next structure:</br></br>             <div class=\"center_text\"> Subject+ <strong>verb to be in present+ verb \u2013ing</strong> + complement</br></br> </div> <span class=\"italic\"> For example: </br> I <strong>am reading</strong> about programming. </br> They <strong>are talking</strong> about object oriented programming. </br> She <strong>is trying</strong> to understand what programming is. </br></br></span>  If you want to formulate a negative statement you just have to add the negative form of the <strong>verb to be</strong> and keep the rest of the structure: </br></br>             <div class=\"center_text\"> Subject+ <strong>verb to be in negative form + verb-ing</strong> + complement</br></br></div>  For example: </br> <span class=\"italic\"> I <strong> am not reading </strong> about programming. </br> They <strong> are not talking </strong> about object oriented programming. </br> She <strong> is not trying </strong> to understand what programming is. </br></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "No, I am not studying. What are you talking about? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We aren't checking complex ideas to understand the concept. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Because we aren't studying from books, let's think about a general and simple example.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Sequence Words", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <strong>sequence words</strong> to link two or more consecutive ideas in a paragraph. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "We need to use sequence words to understand the order in which an event takes place. Look at the following chart; it contains three general parts of a sequence and some of the words that can introduce them. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Beginning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Continuing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Ending \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>First,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>Second, \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>Finally, \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>First of all, \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>Later, \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>To conclude, \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>To begin with,  \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>Next,  \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>In the end,  \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "For example: </br> <span class=\"italic\"> If you want to understand about object oriented programming you need to follow the next process. <strong>First</strong>, read and understand what type of approach it is. <strong>Next,</strong> read about classes and objects, and their importance in this programming. <strong>Finally,</strong> you can try to start solving computation problems to find solutions to a problem. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "First, you describe the car and the person separately; next, you include the methods, and to conclude, you join them together so the person can drive the car from A to B.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "review", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to re-examine and revise ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Laura and I are reviewing our notes about object oriented programming. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "development", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the process of a certain project ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Basically, object oriented programming is an approach to software development, which uses objects to solve different problems.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "solve", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to find a solution to a problem", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Object oriented programming uses objects to solve different problems.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "work", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to operate", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It means that the object knows how the actions of the program work and how the interactions with other components are.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "fulfill", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to accomplish a duty or task ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You need to bring them together so they can interact and fulfill the result you want.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "bring something together", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to join two or more things", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You need to bring them together so they can interact and fulfill the result you want.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go to a library and search additional information on OOP", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Design a brochure about advances on OOP", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your brochure to the class. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I read information about action planning guides", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I design a brochure showing advances on OOP. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my brochure to the class.", "type": "text"}]}]}